WEBVTT

00:06:59.247 --> 00:07:01.892
to change their brains and their behavior,

00:07:01.892 --> 00:07:03.667
for their benefit

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:06.802
and for the benefit of the rest of us.

00:07:06.802 --> 00:07:10.337
So can brains change?

00:07:10.337 --> 00:07:12.921
For over 100 years,

00:07:12.921 --> 00:07:16.035
neuroanatomists and later neuroscientists

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:19.855
held the view that after initial
development in childhood,

00:07:19.855 --> 00:07:22.279
no new brain cells could grow

00:07:22.279 --> 00:07:23.580
in the adult human brain.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.067
The brain could only change

00:07:25.067 --> 00:07:27.049
within certain set limits.

00:07:27.049 --> 00:07:29.147
That was the dogma.

00:07:29.147 --> 00:07:31.386
But then, in the 1990s,